Example: Casual and Sick cannot be combined. Employee applies Sick Mon–Tue, Wed is an institutional holiday, then Casual on Thu — the system still treats this as a restricted combination across the holiday.

Example: Fri Casual, Sat–Sun week-off, Mon Sick with the same rule — the restriction applies across the week-off when this is ON.

When OFF, only directly adjacent calendar dates are used (holidays and week-offs in between are not used to bridge the gap).`,holidayClub:`Sub Rule 1. If 12th August is an Institutional Holiday, then the employee cannot apply for a leave on 13th August.
Sub Rule 2. If 14th August is an Institutional Holiday, then the employee cannot apply for a leave on 13th August.
Sub Rule 3. If 12th and 14th August are both Institutional Holidays, then the employee cannot apply for a leave on 13th August.`,weekOffClub:`Sub Rule 1. If 12th August is a Week Off, then the employee cannot apply for a leave on 13th August.
Sub Rule 2. If 14th August is a Week Off, then the employee cannot apply for a leave on 13th August.
